WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
I'm excited to introduce
Dr. Kristine Dennis,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.120
our new Senior Research Scientist

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.000
who has been researching and
scripting new video topics and,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.640
as you'll hear today,
narrating some as well.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.440
In this video, Kristine
delves into the association

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.480
between vegetarian diets and
hypospadias birth defects

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.604
to see if it holds up in
the light of new research.

00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:32.889
"Pesticide Exposure and Hypospadias
Birth Defects in Vegetarians"

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.200
In 2000, a study found that a
vegetarian diet during pregnancy

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.560
was associated with hypospadias,

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.240
a specific birth defect
of the penis.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.200
The authors suggested
that it may be due

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.640
to the greater exposure
to phytoestrogens,

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.880
which are found in soy foods.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.360
But if you look globally,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.880
while there is
an extraordinarily

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.720
high prevalence
in North America and Europe,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.320
it's extremely low
in a country like Japan,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.000
which has the highest per capita
soy intake in the world.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.200
In fact, in Japan,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.120
a low maternal intake
of soy phytoestrogens

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.600
has been associated with
elevated risk of hypospadias,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.560
so, if anything,
soy may be protective.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.040
If soy foods aren't
the hormone disrupters,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.600
what in a vegetarian diet
might be?

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.880
Well, occupational
exposure to pesticides

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.280
is associated with higher risk,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.480
so, might low-level pesticide
exposure among those eating

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.120
more fruits and vegetables--
like vegetarians--

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:29.920
help explain it?

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.680
If you randomize people

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.280
to a more plant-based
Mediterranean diet,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.680
you see a large increase
in the amount of pesticides

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.840
flowing through their body,
though, of course,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.840
if you put them
on a Mediterranean diet

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.760
with organic fruits
and vegetables,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.160
you see a 90 percent drop
in pesticide exposure.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.120
So, does organic food
consumption during pregnancy

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.560
reduce hypospadias risk?

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.400
Apparently so,
cutting the odds about in half,

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.040
particularly when
it comes to choosing

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.320
organic vegetables and dairy,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.400
though the only other study

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.960
to look at organic food choices
and hypospadias

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.320
found the risk associated

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.000
just with conventional
high-fat dairy products.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.640
It isn't all or nothing.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.560
Even if only two thirds
of your produce is organic,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.720
that can significantly reduce
pesticide exposure,

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.760
but the benefits of consuming
conventionally grown produce

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.920
likely outweigh any possible
risks from pesticide exposure,

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.080
so, concerns over
ingesting pesticides

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.840
should never discourage
fruit and vegetable intake.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.800
In the United States alone,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.440
if you add up all
of the fatal cancers, strokes,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.280
heart attacks, and other deaths
that could have been averted

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.920
simply by eating
more fruits and vegetables,

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.840
it comes out to nearly
450,000 deaths every year.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.320
That's how powerful
produce can be.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.920
But might one of the downsides
be this hypospadias risk?

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.960
Despite their high
plant consumption,

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.880
vegetarians may be less exposed
to conventional pesticides,

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.600
but that's because
of their greater propensity

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.280
to choose organic produce.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.440
Now, the researchers only
considered the pesticides

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.080
in plant foods,
not animal products,

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.280
and even for
conventional insecticides,

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.840
animal products are
main contributors to exposure.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.960
Additionally,
persistent pesticides,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.320
such as organochlorine
pesticides like DDT,

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.960
are concentrated in fish,
other meats, and dairy,

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:22.960
so it's no surprise

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.840
that the blood of
strictly plant-based eaters

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.000
ends up significantly
less polluted.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.840
It may not just be from the
lower level of intake, though;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.080
high fiber diets can bulk up the
stool and glom on to pesticides

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.760
and flush them away.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.640
In the end, the hypospadias
issue may be another example

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.160
of the stroke scare.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.400
Dr. Greger did a whole series
covering potential explanations

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.320
why a study had found higher
stroke rates among vegetarians,

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.080
but then, half a dozen
other studies found

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:57.560
lower rates of stroke,
if anything, across the board.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.240
The original hypospadias study
looked at about 50 cases.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.240
Twelve years later,

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:06.560
a study that looked
at 1,250 cases was published

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:11.258
and found zero increased risk
among vegetarian mothers.

